   "text": "[Heading: Heating circuit failure (E:09)]\nThe E:09 error on your Bosch dishwasher specifically points to a fault in the flow-through heating element or its associated circuit. Regarding cost: this is generally a moderate repair rather than an expensive one. The most likely faulty component is the heating element itself, which is a standard replacement part. However, it can sometimes be the relay on the main control board that switches the heater on. Because this involves internal electrical components and water, I recommend calling a qualified appliance engineer to diagnose and replace the faulty part safely."
